      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-15170",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose that\n$S = \u2211_(n = 2)^(\u221e)((-1)^{n})/(\\ln (n))$\nand that $s_{9}$ is the ninth partial sum of $S$. According to the alternating series error bound, $\\mid S - s_{9} \\mid < k$ for some real number $k$. Find the value of $k$."
