      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50830",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose that\n$S = \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)((-1)^{n}n)/(n!)$\nand that $s_{5}$ is the fifth partial sum of $S$. According to the alternating series error bound, $\\mid S - s_{5} \\mid < k$ for some real number $k$. Find the value of $k$."
